  "idea": {
    "name": "Everything Down Here Makes Its Own Light",
    "premise": "Below the meadow there is a trench the moon cannot reach, and nothing there has ever seen light it did not make itself. But the trench is only the edge. Past it lies the abyssal plain, where marine snow falls forever onto black silt and a lighthouse that fell in a storm lies drowned on its side, still turning, nobody having told it there are no ships. Out there something has begun to answer. Every flash sent into the dark comes back late, in a slightly different colour, and nobody can tell whether the reply is kindness or hunger. The house is about loneliness that learns to glow, and the worse hope that follows: being answered, and not being able to stop.",
